---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const SECTIONS = [
  { id: 'remote-access', title: 'Remote Access VPN' },
  { id: 'site-to-site', title: 'Site-to-Site VPN' },
  { id: 'cloud-vpn', title: 'Cloud VPN' },
  { id: 'mobile-vpn', title: 'Mobile VPN' },
  { id: 'ssl-tls', title: 'SSL/TLS VPN' },
  { id: 'split-tunnel', title: 'Split Tunnel VPN' },
];
---

<Layout title="6 Types of VPN — Cheatsheet" description="Six VPN types explained: Remote Access, Site-to-Site, Cloud VPN, Mobile VPN, SSL/TLS VPN, and Split Tunneling — use cases, strengths, and illustrations.">
  <main>
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
      <a href="/cheatsheet" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm mb-8" style="color: var(--accent)">
        ← back to cheatsheets
      </a>

      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest px-3 py-1 rounded-full" style="background: var(--accent); color: #1a1a1a">Security</span>
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest px-3 py-1 rounded-full" style="background: var(--bg-surface); color: var(--text-muted)">VPN</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="font-black uppercase tracking-tight mb-2" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); line-height: 0.95">
        6 Types of <span style="color: var(--accent)">VPN</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm mb-6" style="color: var(--text-muted)">Know the difference. Choose the right one. Security and performance both depend on it.</p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8 text-xs font-mono" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
        <span>8 min read</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>6 sections</span>
      </div>

      <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-10 text-xs font-mono">
        {SECTIONS.map(s => (
          <li>
            <a href={"#" + s.id} class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full border transition-colors" style="border-color: var(--border); color: var(--text-muted)">
              {s.title}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <div id="remote-access" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#remote-access" class="hover-underline">1. Remote Access VPN</a>
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted)">Connects individual users to a private network from a remote location.</p>
            <p class="font-bold mt-2" style="color: var(--accent)">Best for remote employees</p>
            <ul class="mt-2" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
              <li>✓ Most common type</li>
              <li>✓ Used by remote employees to access company systems securely</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2 flex items-center justify-center" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <div class="text-center">
              <div class="text-xs font-mono" style="color: var(--text-faint)">Remote User → Internet → Company Network</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="site-to-site" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#site-to-site" class="hover-underline">2. Site-to-Site VPN</a>
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted)">Links two or more entire office networks together over the internet.</p>
            <p class="font-bold mt-2" style="color: var(--accent)">Great for multi-branch enterprises</p>
            <ul class="mt-2" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
              <li>✓ Ideal for enterprises with multiple branches</li>
              <li>✓ No per-user setup needed</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2 flex items-center justify-center" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <div class="text-center">
              <div class="text-xs font-mono" style="color: var(--text-faint)">Office A → Internet → Office B</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="cloud-vpn" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#cloud-vpn" class="hover-underline">3. Cloud VPN</a>
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted)">Secures connections between users/offices and cloud platforms like AWS, Azure, or GCP.</p>
            <p class="font-bold mt-2" style="color: var(--accent)">Built for the cloud era</p>
            <ul class="mt-2" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
              <li>✓ A must-have as businesses move workloads off on-prem servers</li>
              <li>✓ Connects to AWS, Azure, GCP, and other cloud platforms</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2 flex items-center justify-center" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <div class="text-center">
              <div class="text-xs font-mono" style="color: var(--text-faint)">Users/Offices → Internet → Cloud Platforms</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="mobile-vpn" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#mobile-vpn" class="hover-underline">4. Mobile VPN</a>
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted)">Maintains a stable encrypted tunnel even when devices switch networks (WiFi → 4G → 5G).</p>
            <p class="font-bold mt-2" style="color: var(--accent)">Perfect for people on the move</p>
            <ul class="mt-2" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
              <li>✓ Built for field workers, first responders</li>
              <li>✓ Ideal for mobile-heavy teams</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2 flex items-center justify-center" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <div class="text-center">
              <div class="text-xs font-mono" style="color: var(--text-faint)">Mobile User (WiFi/4G/5G) → Internet → Company Network</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="ssl-tls" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#ssl-tls" class="hover-underline">5. SSL/TLS VPN</a>
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted)">Runs entirely through a web browser using HTTPS — no software installation required.</p>
            <p class="font-bold mt-2" style="color: var(--accent)">No installs. Just open and connect.</p>
            <ul class="mt-2" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
              <li>✓ Perfect for contractors or BYOD environments</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2 flex items-center justify-center" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <div class="text-center">
              <div class="text-xs font-mono" style="color: var(--text-faint)">Web Browser → HTTPS → Company Network</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="split-tunnel" class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black uppercase tracking-wide mb-3" style="color: var(--text)">
          <a href="#split-tunnel" class="hover-underline">6. Split Tunnel VPN</a>
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted)">Routes only specific traffic through the VPN; the rest goes through the regular internet.</p>
            <p class="font-bold mt-2" style="color: var(--accent)">Smarter routing. Better performance.</p>
            <ul class="mt-2" style="color: var(--text-muted)">
              <li>✓ Reduces bandwidth load</li>
              <li>✓ Improves speed without sacrificing key security</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border-2 flex items-center justify-center" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
            <div class="text-center">
              <div class="text-xs font-mono" style="color: var(--text-faint)">Work Traffic → VPN | Other Traffic → Internet</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 p-4 rounded-xl border-2 text-center" style="background: var(--bg-card); border-color: var(--border)">
        <p class="text-xs font-mono" style="color: var(--text-faint)">
          VPN is not one size fits all. The right type depends on your users, network design, cloud usage, and security requirements.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 text-center">
        <a href="/" class="inline-block px-6 py-3 font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-sm border-2 transition-all" style="background: var(--accent); color: #1a1a1a; border-color: #1a1a1a; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 #1a1a1a; border-radius: 9999px">
          ← all cheatsheets
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.talz.net" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Cheatsheets", "item": "https://www.talz.net/cheatsheet/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "VPN Types Cheatsheet", "item": "https://www.talz.net/cheatsheet/vpn-types/" }
    ]
  })} />
</Layout>
